# SaaS Context for <%= app_name %>

Complete SaaS setup with subscriptions, billing, multi-tenancy, and team management.

## What's Included

### Skills
- **rails-models** - Account, subscription, plan, membership models
- **rails-controllers** - Account management, billing, team controllers
- **rails-views** - Dashboard, settings, billing pages
- **rails-auth-with-devise** - User authentication
- **rails-jobs** - Background jobs for webhooks and billing
- **rails-mailers** - Trial, payment, and team invitation emails

### Agent
- **saas-dev** - SaaS development specialist

## Getting Started

### 1. Install Stripe

```bash
echo "gem 'stripe'" >> Gemfile
bundle install

rails credentials:edit
# Add: stripe: { publishable_key: xxx, secret_key: xxx, webhook_secret: xxx }
```

### 2. Generate Models

```bash
# Multi-tenancy
rails g model Account name:string subdomain:string:uniq owner_id:integer settings:jsonb

rails g model Membership account:references user:references role:string

# Subscriptions
rails g model Plan name:string price:decimal interval:string trial_days:integer \
  stripe_price_id:string features_json:text

rails g model Subscription account:references plan:references \
  status:string stripe_subscription_id:string stripe_customer_id:string \
  trial_ends_at:datetime current_period_start:datetime current_period_end:datetime
```

### 3. Configure Subdomain Routing

```ruby
# config/routes.rb
Rails.application.routes.draw do
  constraints subdomain: /.+/ do
    # Account-scoped routes
    resources :projects
    resources :team_members
    resource :billing
  end

  # Root domain routes
  root 'marketing#index'
  devise_for :users
end
```

### 4. Set Up Stripe Webhooks

```bash
# Development
stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/webhooks/stripe

# Production - configure in Stripe Dashboard
https://yourapp.com/webhooks/stripe
```

## Key Features

- [ ] User authentication with Devise
- [ ] Account creation and subdomain setup
- [ ] Subscription plans (Starter, Pro, Enterprise)
- [ ] Stripe checkout integration
- [ ] Trial period (14 days)
- [ ] Team member invitations
- [ ] Role-based permissions
- [ ] Usage tracking and limits
- [ ] Billing management (update card, invoices)
- [ ] Admin dashboard

